abstract: >-
  A practical Quality Engineering framework for evaluating large language model
  applications across correctness, relevance, completeness, groundedness,
  citations, safety, privacy, refusal behavior, structured output, robustness,
  stability, latency, token usage, cost and regression risk. The work advocates
  versioned evaluation datasets, deterministic-first metrics, calibrated model
  judges, candidate-versus-baseline comparison, explicit release policies and
  CI/CD quality gates.